h libraries are `dlopen`ed via `libloading`; the Rust function is only ever reached through its `#[no_mangle]` export.\n- Since stdout *is* the function's result, the harness redirects fd 1 to a temp file (not a pipe — batches run to megabytes) and compares bytes. Batch-compare first, then bisect to name the exact diverging input.\n- ~60k randomized inputs from a fixed-seed SplitMix64, plus two exhaustive 2048-exponent sweeps.\n- **Negative control run**: I temporarily changed the Rust format to `%.5f`; the suite immediately failed with per-input `DIVERGENCE` reports on 20+ rows, confirming the harness isn't trivially passing. `lib.rs` was restored from backup.\n\n`./translation/run_all.sh` reproduces everything. Two caveats worth flagging: crates.io is unreachable in this sandbox, so all cargo commands use `--offline` against the cached `libloading 0.8.9`; and tests must run with `--test-threads=1` because fd-1 redirection is process-global (the harness also holds a mutex as a backstop)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":542,"cache_read_input_tokens":71113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":542,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f87226e-694a-4c15-8600-9c2973c6c010","uuid":"661b8ff9-3f3d-4882-9a2f-07140e7f7d98","timestamp":"2026-09-05T05:32:13.561Z"}
