ass |\n| Phase D — symbol diff | ✅ empty (C exports 1 symbol `driver`; Rust exports it) |\n| Binary stdout compare | vacuous — neither project builds an executable |\n| All feature combos × dev/release | ✅ 8/8 configurations pass |\n\n## Phase A findings\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`**: C `.so` exports exactly one real symbol, `driver`. No untranslated module — `CMakeLists.txt` lists one source file, fully covered by `src/lib.rs`. Rust imports resolve entirely against glibc.\n- **`ERRORS.md`**: the error table is **empty** — grepping the whole C source finds 0 `return`s, 0 error macros, 0 `assert`s, 0 range/null checks, 0 branches. `driver` is a total function. The phase obligation was redischarged against 9 generic-boundary rows (E1–E9), with each N/A case documented as to *why* (no pointer param, no length param, no enum param) and mapped to its nearest real analogue.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`**: no runtime options exist, so the only axis is the `double`'s shape — 22 rows covering signed zeros, all 2048 exponent fields, subnormals, `%a` trailing-zero trimming, `%.4f` tie/carry cases, infinities, sNaN/qNaN payloads, raw `u64` patterns, and stateful/interleaved use.\n\n## Testing notes\n\n- Both libraries are `dlopen`ed via `libloading`; the Rust function is only ever reached through its `#[no_mangle]` export.\n- Since stdout *is* the function's result, the harness redirects fd 1 to a temp file (not a pipe — batches run to megabytes) and compares bytes. Batch-compare first, then bisect to name the exact diverging input.\n- ~60k randomized inputs from a fixed-seed SplitMix64, plus two exhaustive 2048-exponent sweeps.\n- **Negative control run**: I temporarily changed the Rust format to `%.5f`; the suite immediately failed with per-input `DIVERGENCE` reports on 20+ rows, confirming the harness isn't trivially passing. `lib.rs` was restored from backup.\n\n`./translation/run_all.sh` reproduces everything. Two caveats worth flagging: crates.io is unreachable in this sandbox, so all cargo commands use `--offline` against the cached `libloading 0.8.9`; and tests must run with `--test-threads=1` because fd-1 redirection is process-global (the harness also holds a mutex as a backstop).","ttft_ms":2568,"type":"result","duration_ms":511792,"uuid":"47ee314e-e7fd-4a7a-b2a5-46d5bf36a3b1","ttft_stream_ms":2445,"time_to_request_ms":91,"first_content_frame_ms":2445,"queued_turn_count":0}
